Story 1: Product Activation

As part of introducing the new IELTS on Paper (IOP) product, we successfully activated it across lower and production environments. This foundational step ensured that IOP is now recognized within our platform, enabling us to proceed with its full integration across systems. Activation was critical to initiate visibility, configuration, and eventual operational readiness across all user interfaces and services.
Story 2: View & Configure IOP Products

Once activated, we enhanced the CMDS UI to support the viewing and configuration of IOP products. Now, as IELTS Global Ops users, we can see IOP alongside existing products within the product management screen, configure authorizations, and manage their availability for specific Test Centres and Physical Buildings. This enabled granular product control through a user-friendly interface.
Story 3: Cascade Product Approvals

To reduce operational overhead and eliminate manual effort, we implemented cascading logic for product approvals. Now, when a product like IOP is approved for a Test Centre, the approval automatically cascades to all of its associated Physical Buildings. This feature ensures consistency, speeds up rollout, and minimizes the risk of human error during product assignment.
Story 4: RBAC Permissions for Allocation Groups and Products

We introduced robust role-based access control (RBAC) to manage who can view and perform actions on Allocation Groups and IOP products. This includes defining granular CRUD permissions for users, ensuring only authorized individuals can add, modify, or delete allocation data. It adds a security layer and aligns access with user roles and responsibilities.
Story 5: Create & View Allocation Groups

Building on the RBAC foundation, we developed features that allow authorized users to create new Allocation Groups by specifying their names and statuses. In addition, a view-all page was implemented where users can see a list of all configured groups, allowing them to filter, search, and monitor group configurations across the system.
Story 6: Edit & View Individual Allocation Group Details

Finally, we enhanced the Allocation Group experience by adding edit capabilities and detailed views. Users with appropriate permissions can now update group information or click into any group to see its specific assignments and metadata. This supports better group lifecycle management and provides full visibility into allocation strategies.
